X-Rates Historical Currency Scraper
===================================

Historical Exchange Rate Scraper using BeautifulSoup and Pandas

Overview
--------

X-Rates Scraper is a simple Python application that retrieves historical
exchange rates from x-rates.com and exports them into a CSV file.

The application accepts a base currency and a date range, downloads the
historical exchange rate table for each day, parses the HTML using
BeautifulSoup, and stores the collected data using Pandas.

Repository Structure
--------------------

x-rates-scraper/
├── output/                # Generated CSV files
├── .dockerignore
├── .gitignore
├── .python-version
├── compose.yaml
├── Dockerfile
├── LICENSE
├── README.md
├── main.py
├── pyproject.toml
└── uv.lock

Requirements
------------

* Python 3.12+
* uv
* Docker (Optional)

Installation
------------

Clone the repository.

    git clone https://github.com/princesingh-ai/x-rates-scraper.git

Move into the project directory.

    cd x-rates-scraper

Install the project dependencies.

    uv sync

Running
-------

Run the application.

    uv run python main.py

Example

    Currency: USD
    Start Date (YYYY-MM-DD): 2024-01-01
    End Date (YYYY-MM-DD): 2024-01-07

The generated CSV file will be saved in:

    output/

Docker
------

Build the image.

    docker build -t x-rates-scraper .

Run the container.

    docker run -it \
    -v $(pwd)/output:/app/output \
    x-rates-scraper

Docker Compose
--------------

Build
    docker compose build

Run
    docker compose run --rm xrates-scraper

